oined U-KISS in November 2009, before departing the group in May 2019 and later rejoining the group in January 2022.","title":"Lee Ki-seop","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lee_Ki-seop"}},"Q28826153":{"id":"Q28826153","name":"BM","ko":"","birthName":"Kim Jin-suk","birthNameEn":"Kim Jin-suk","aliases":["Matthew Kim","Big Matthew"],"birth":"1992-10-20","death":"","birthplace":"Los Angeles","nationality":["United States","South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["rapper","singer","songwriter","dancer"],"debut":"2016","agencies":[{"name":"DSP Media","korean":true,"id":"Q489428","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q27989963","name":"KARD","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/bigmatthewww/","x":"https://x.com/kard_bigmatthew","tiktok":"https://www.tiktok.com/@bigmattheww","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5lZV4z4dpX6IfTYlfUMvOE","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/5736c306-d717-4c96-be64-15c68df606c9"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Matthew Kim, known by his stage name BM or Big Matthew, is an American rapper, songwriter, composer, and actor based in South Korea signed under DSP Media. He is best known as a member of the co-ed group Kard. He made his debut as a solo artist on June 9, 2021, with the single \"Broken Me\".","title":"BM (rapper)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BM_%28rapper%29"}},"Q43089385":{"id":"Q43089385","name":"NAVINCI","ko":"","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Kim Min-sung","Hansol"],"birth":"1993-06-15","death":"","birthplace":"Busan","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2012","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q15633507","name":"Xeno-T","start":"2013","end":"2017"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/navinci_casso/","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCofbPbAvp7wwSZof8QgfXeg"},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q43111017":{"id":"Q43111017","name":"Minseo","ko":"민서","birthName":"Kim Min-seo","birthNameEn":"Kim Min-seo","aliases":[],"birth":"1996-04-09","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","actor"],"debut":"2018","agencies":[{"name":"Mystic Story","korean":true,"id":"Q15509774","start":"","end":""},{"name":"Kakao M","korean":true,"id":"Q625975","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/minse0_96/","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCsV2Muttx7rV9s6mtHHwhHw","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/95a40af6-1d95-4c2a-a607-73a2c59c0d56"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Kim Min-seo, known mononymously as Minseo, is a South Korean singer and actress. She was selected as part of the Top 8 on Superstar K 7. She made her official debut in 2018 with \"Wonderful Dream\".","title":"Minseo (singer, born 1996)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minseo_%28singer%2C_born_1996%29"}},"Q43111145":{"id":"Q43111145","name":"Ahin","ko":"아인","birthName":"이아인","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Lee Ah-in"],"birth":"1999-09-27","death":"","birthplace":"Ulsan","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q27820706","name":"Momoland","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/heyitsahin_/","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/f611ae1f-1a13-4bcd-8d74-42153aa6d163"},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q47690025":{"id":"Q47690025","name":"Johnny Suh","ko":"쟈니","birthName":"John Seo","birthNameEn":"John Seo","aliases":["Johnny","John Seo"],"birth":"1995-02-09","death":"","birthplace":"Chicago","nationality":["United States","South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["rapper","YouTuber","dancer","singer"],"debut":"2017","agencies":[{"name":"SM Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q483938","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q23725822","name":"NCT","start":"2017","end":""},{"id":"Q67972645","name":"NCT U","start":"2017","end":""},{"id":"Q55624444","name":"NCT 127","start":"2017","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/johnnyjsuh/","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/7Gt75izt6biWaQDeWN9jF2","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/79204093-5fae-4a73-9f02-7d602444f7dd"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"John Jeon Suh, known professionally as Johnny, is an American singer, rapper, and television personality. He rose to prominence as a member of the K-pop boy band NCT and its sub-unit NCT 127. Born and raised in Chicago, Johnny started training in South Korea under SM Entertainment in 2007. He began his career in 2013 as part of the label's official team of trainees, SM Rookies, appearing on television and touring both in the country and abroad. He made his debut in 2017 with NCT, which went on to achieve commercial success and become an influential K-pop act. Beyond his music career, Johnny has also hosted web shows and ventured into television, appearing on several variety shows.","title":"Johnny (singer)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johnny_%28singer%29"}},"Q490153":{"id":"Q490153","name":"Kim Wan-sun","ko":"김완선","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Kim Wansun","Kim Wan Sun","Kim Wan-seon","Kim Wan Seon","Kim Wanseon","Kim I-sun","Kim I Sun","Kim Isun"],"birth":"1969-05-16","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"1986","agencies":[],"groups":[],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/kimwansunflower/","x":"https://x.com/ppurple516","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCeUgLKBHMTjpi2p4J1LbDoQ","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/813d3000-8751-4dbb-a35f-f490f2637f2e"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Kim Wan-sun is a South Korean pop singer who was known in the mid-1980s and early 1990s as the \"Korean Madonna\" and \"the dancing queen of Korean popular music's renaissance era\" as well as a sex symbol for her \"sexy\" dancing and \"charismatic\" stage presence. Kim debuted in 1986 with the album, Tonight. Her fifth album, 1990's Pierrot Smiles at Us, sold 1 million copies. She is considered to be one of the first wave of Hallyu artists due to her success in Taiwan in the mid-1990s.","title":"Kim Wan-sun","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kim_Wan-sun"}},"Q55736873":{"id":"Q55736873","name":"Daewon","ko":"대원 (가수)","birthName":"박대원","birthNameEn":"","aliases":[],"birth":"1992-03-17","death":"","birthplace":"Cheonan","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q18712427","name":"Madtown","start":"","end":""},{"id":"Q48938268","name":"UNB","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/dw_317/","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/38f17cfa-8767-41cc-9027-edd9b73a2c31"},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q60668841":{"id":"Q60668841","name":"Bang Hyun-ah","ko":"방현아","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Lina","Lin Ah"],"birth":"1991-02-27","death":"","birthplace":"Incheon","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q28700240","name":"WANNA.B","start":"2016","end":""}],"links":{},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q61679273":{"id":"Q61679273","name":"Seung-hwa Park","ko":"박승화 (가수)","birthName":"박승진","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Park Seung Hwa"],"birth":"1969-03-11","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q8061687","name":"Yurisangja","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/f46faa51-ba65-460c-ad25-bdf3d96fcf41"},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q61770153":{"id":"Q61770153","name":"Kim Do-ah","ko":"도아","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Doah"],"birth":"2003-12-04","death":"","birthplace":"South Korea","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2018","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q60643800","name":"Fanatics","start":"2018","end":""},{"id":"Q60992623","name":"Flavor","start":"2018","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/lcirndxah/","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/c11c5f61-b515-4948-bda8-2de4bd3f3ab3"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1f/190823_%EB%8F%84%EC%95%84_Kim_Do-ah.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:190823_%EB%8F%84%EC%95%84_Kim_Do-ah.png","author":"NewsInstar","license":"CC BY 3.0"},"bio":{"text":"Kim Do-ah, also known by the mononym Doah, is a South Korean singer, rapper, and actress. She was a member of South Korean girl group, Fanatics and its sub-unit, Fanatics-Flavor until their disbandment in 2024. She is known for her participation in Produce 48 and Girls Planet 999.","title":"Kim Do-ah","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kim_Do-ah"}},"Q62984297":{"id":"Q62984297","name":"Soon Min-ji","ko":"손민지","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Ayeon"],"birth":"2002-09-29","death":"","birthplace":"South Korea","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q60992060","name":"Saturday","start":"","end":""}],"links":{},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q6362153":{"id":"Q6362153","name":"Brave Brothers","ko":"용감한 형제","birthName":"강동철","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Kang Dong-chul","Brave Sound"],"birth":"1979-06-07","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["rapper","songwriter","record producer"],"debut":"2002","agencies":[{"name":"YG Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q50595","start":"","end":""},{"name":"Brave Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q4958352","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/bravebrosyh/","x":"https://x.com/bravebros","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/846bd846-c7d9-460f-ba17-b7778dccc127"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Kang Dong-chul, also known by his stage name Brave Brothers, is a South Korean rapper, record producer and songwriter for Brave Entertainment. He was a producer and composer for YG Entertainment from 2004 to 2008. In 2008, he started his own record label called Brave Entertainment. He has produced hit songs for After School, Sistar, 4Minute, T-ara, Son Dam Bi, Big Bang, Brown Eyed Girls, AOA, Hello Venus, RANIA and U-KISS. In 2009, he made his music debut with Attitude and later released Passionate on December 8. His label manages acts such as Electroboyz, BIGSTAR, and DKB. Kang was a judge panelist on JTBC's Made In U program in 2011.","title":"Brave Brothers","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brave_Brothers"}},"Q6762473":{"id":"Q6762473","name":"Hong Yoo-kyung","ko":"홍유경","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":[],"birth":"1994-09-22","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q483286","name":"Apink","start":"2011","end":"2013"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/yukyung_922/","x":"https://x.com/Apinkhyk","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/ec157ee3-d84d-4682-8d81-7b60c001b2bc"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Apink is a South Korean girl group formed in 2011, currently consists of five members: Chorong, Bomi, Eunji, Namjoo, and Hayoung. Apink was originally a septet; Yookyung left in 2013 to pursue her education and Naeun left to pursue her acting career in 2022. The group debuted on April 19, 2011, with the extended play (EP) Seven Springs of Apink. Since their debut, Apink has won awards at shows such as the Golden Disc Awards, the Seoul Music Awards and the Mnet Asian Music Awards. Their first music program win was on M Countdown on January 5, 2012, for \"My My\" from their second EP Snow Pink.","title":"Hong Yoo-kyung","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hong_Yoo-kyung"}},"Q67991401":{"id":"Q67991401","name":"Oh Heejun","ko":"오희준","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Heejun","Woo Je-yeon"],"birth":"1996-05-08","death":"","b